// SR 910.12 — Section 2a: Temporary Suspension of Individual Provisions of the Product Specification
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
Inserted by No I of the O of 1 Nov. 2023, in force since 1 Jan. 2024 (AS 2023 697).
|

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 14a
1 The Federal Department of Economic Affairs, Education and Research (EAER) may in the following cases authorise by means of an ordinance a temporary suspension of individual provisions of the product specification that are set out in Article 7 paragraph 1 letters c and d:
a. in the case of extraordinary natural events that prevent compliance with specific points of the product specification for a specific period;
b. in response to official decisions based on federal or canton law, in particular relating to public or plant health, that prevent compliance with specific points of the product specification for a specific period.
2 The group shall apply to FOAG for a temporary suspension. The application must be accompanied by proof that the application has been approved by the representatives’ meeting of the group.
3 The group must prove that temporary suspension will have no direct effects on the principal physical, chemical, microbiological and organoleptic properties of the products or on its specific shape.
4 It must prove that appropriate measures are being taken to inform the public or the end consumers of the temporary suspension of the provisions.
5 The EAER may stipulate additional terms and conditions for the temporary suspension of provisions. In particular, it may restrict the suspension to part of the geographical area.
6 The temporary suspension may not last for more than one year; it may only be extended on the same grounds on one occasion.

